# Agile and TDD (this repo)

Tracker: GitHub Issues. Integration branch: `develop`. Stable branch: `main`.

## One issue

- Branch from `develop`: `feature/<issue>-slug` or `bugfix/<issue>-slug`.
- Pull request targets `develop`. Do not push feature work straight to `main`.
- Do not open a second in-progress issue. Do not mark the issue Done; QA owns that.

## Story before code

```
User Story
As a <role>, I want <capability>, so that <value>.

Acceptance Criteria
Given <context>
When <action>
Then <outcome>
```

## TDD

Functional Rust only. Config, docs, and workflow YAML skip the red-green cycle; say so.

1. RED — one or two assertions, expected value explicit. `cargo test -p <crate> <test_name>`. Confirm the failure reason.
2. GREEN — production code only. Re-run the same test.
3. REFACTOR — names and duplication only. Re-run `cargo test --workspace --exclude gamefocus-ui`.

Do not delete, weaken, or empty an assertion to get green. The terminal log is the exit criterion.

Suggested commit: `test:`, `feat:`, or `fix:` with `(RED)` / `(GREEN)` / `(REFACTOR)` when the user asked to commit. Do not commit unless asked.
